<title>SOUTH AFRICA: LTA lifts yr shr, div increased.</title>
<headline>LTA lifts yr shr, div increased.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   191.0	  vs     161.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  48.0	  vs	40.0</p>
<p>    Net earnings	    53.74	  vs     45.55</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   96.35	  vs     76.10</p>
<p>    Tax			 32.87	  vs     22.34</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    0.16	  vs     0.82 received</p>
<p>    Turnover	     3,016.00	  vs     2,511.00</p>
<p>Div payable April 11</p>
<p>on register March 7</p>
<p>Full name: LTA Ltd (building and construction)</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast LTA Ltd's earnings rising to between 189 and 191 cents with consensus at 190.2 cents from 162.0 cents a year ago.</p>
<p>They put the dividend at between 65 and 69 cents with consensus at 66.6 versus 57.5 cents before.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
